---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config/site";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Known issues"
  description={`Confirmed limitations in the current ${siteConfig.productName} founding-beta build, dated and updated as fixes ship.`}
  lastUpdated={siteConfig.knownIssuesUpdated}
>
  <p>
    This list covers confirmed, current limitations of the founding-beta
    build — not a general roadmap. It is updated as issues are fixed or new
    ones are found. If you hit something not listed here, tell us:{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`}>{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Scope limitations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Managed Library mode is disabled.</strong> An internal audit
      found a data-safety issue where an interrupted Managed-mode import
      could resume incorrectly and report false completion. Reference
      Library mode does not have this issue and is the only mode available
      in the founding beta.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>MP3 export is disabled.</strong> Third-party licensing for the
      bundled MP3 encoder has not been cleared for commercial distribution.
      WAV, AIFF, FLAC, and M4A export remain available. MP3 import is
      unaffected.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Multi-item drag-and-drop is not yet available.</strong>{" "}
      Dragging one sample at a time into your DAW or Finder is supported;
      dragging multiple selected items at once needs further work.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No automatic updates.</strong> New builds during the beta are
      sent manually by the founder with update instructions.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>External drives</h2>
  <p>
    Reference libraries on external SSDs are supported and are the expected
    setup for large libraries, but the drive-safety test matrix is not yet
    exhaustive:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Hands-on testing across eject, reconnect, permission revocation,
      sleep/wake, a changed mount path, and swapping in a same-named
      replacement volume is ongoing rather than fully automated.
    </li>
    <li>
      If a drive disconnects mid-analysis, the in-flight file's result may
      wait for that specific operation to finish before the app visibly
      pauses.
    </li>
    <li>
      Free-disk-space is checked before an operation starts, but if space
      changes mid-operation on a nearly-full removable volume, behavior
      under that specific condition is still being verified.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Performance at large scale</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Batch edits (tags, ratings, color labels) across very large
      multi-selections may be slower than in later releases. Ordinary
      selections are unaffected; a safe limit or warning applies to
      pathological cases.
    </li>
    <li>
      Extremely long individual audio files — beyond roughly 30 minutes or
      requiring more than 1&nbsp;GB of decoded audio — are rejected by a
      safety guardrail rather than processed. This does not affect ordinary
      samples and loops.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Accessibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Sonic Map is rendered on a canvas surface, and full VoiceOver support
      for that view is not yet complete. Search, library management, and
      audition are keyboard- and VoiceOver-accessible.
    </li>
  </ul>
</LegalLayout>
